<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">26</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sentinum"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Sentinum</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 295 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Sentinum was fought in 295 BCE near Sentinum in Umbria, close to modern Sassoferrato, between Rome and a coalition of Samnites and Senone Gauls, with…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yique"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Yique</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 293 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Yique was fought in 293 BCE near Luoyang, in present-day Henan, between the State of Qin and the allied armies of Han and Wei.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-corupedium"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-corupedium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Corupedium</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 281 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Corupedium was fought in 281 BCE in western Anatolia between Seleucus I and Lysimachus, two of Alexander's successors.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-beneventum-275-bc"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Beneventum (275 BC)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 275 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Beneventum was fought in southern Italy in 275 BCE between a Roman army under the consul Manius Curius Dentatus and Pyrrhus of Epirus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-changping"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-changping.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Changping</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 262–260 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Changping, fought from 262 to 260 BCE near present-day Gaoping in Shanxi, was the decisive clash between the Chinese states of Qin and Zhao.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-longanus-river"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Longanus River</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 260s BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Longanus River was fought in north-eastern Sicily in the 260s BCE between Hieron II of Syracuse and the Mamertines, Campanian mercenaries who held…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-aegates"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Aegates</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 241 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Aegates was a naval battle fought in 241 BCE off the western coast of Sicily, in which the Roman fleet defeated the Carthaginian navy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ladoceia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-ladoceia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ladoceia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 227 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ladoceia was fought in 227 BCE near Megalopolis in Arcadia during the Cleomenean War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-hekatombaion"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Hekatombaion</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 226 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Hekatombaion was fought in 226 BCE near Dyme in western Achaea, where Cleomenes III of Sparta crushed the full army of the Achaean League.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-telamon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-telamon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Telamon</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 225 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Telamon was fought in 225 BCE near Telamon on the coast of Etruria between the Roman Republic and an invading army of Gauls from northern Italy, led by…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-clastidium"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-clastidium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Clastidium</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 222 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Clastidium was fought in 222 BCE near Clastidium, modern Casteggio in Lombardy, between the Roman Republic and the Insubres with their Gaesatae allies.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sellasia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-sellasia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Sellasia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 222 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Sellasia was fought in 222 BCE north of Sparta, where Antigonus III Doson of Macedon and the Achaean League defeated King Cleomenes III of Sparta.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cissa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-cissa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Cissa</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 218 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Cissa was fought in 218 BCE near the town of Cissa, north of Tarraco in north-eastern Spain, early in the Second Punic War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-trebia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-trebia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Trebia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 218 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Trebia was fought in 218 BCE in northern Italy, the first major victory of Hannibal over the Romans after his crossing of the Alps during the Second…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lake-trasimene"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-lake-trasimene.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Lake Trasimene</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 217 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Lake Trasimene was fought in 217 BCE in central Italy during the Second Punic War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-raphia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-raphia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Raphia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 217 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Raphia was fought in 217 BCE near Gaza during the Fourth Syrian War, between Ptolemy IV of Egypt and the Seleucid king Antiochus III.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cannae"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-cannae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Cannae</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 216 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Cannae was fought in 216 BCE in south-eastern Italy during the Second Punic War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-julu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-julu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Julu</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 207 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Julu was fought in 207 BCE near Julu, in present-day Hebei, between rebel forces led by Xiang Yu and the Qin armies besieging the city.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mantinea-207-bce"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Mantinea (207 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 207 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Mantinea of 207 BCE was fought in Arcadia between the Achaean League under Philopoemen and the Spartans under Machanidas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ilipa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-ilipa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ilipa</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 206 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ilipa was fought in 206 BCE near Ilipa, north of Seville in southern Spain, during the Second Punic War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chenggao"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Chenggao</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 204–203 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Chenggao was a prolonged struggle in 204–203 BCE between Liu Bang of Han and Xiang Yu of Chu for the strategic town of Chenggao, near the Ao granary in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jingxing"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Jingxing</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 204 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Jingxing was fought in 204 BCE at the Jingxing pass in the Taihang Mountains, in present-day Hebei, during the Chu–Han Contention.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-great-plains"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-great-plains.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Great Plains</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 203 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Great Plains was fought in 203 BCE in the Bagradas valley of North Africa, in present-day Tunisia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaixia"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Gaixia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 202 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Gaixia, fought in 202 BCE in what is now Anhui province, was the final battle of the Chu–Han Contention.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-zama"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-zama.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Zama</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 202 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Zama, fought in 202 BCE in present-day Tunisia, was the decisive battle of the Second Punic War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-baideng"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Baideng</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 200 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Baideng took place in 200 BCE near present-day Datong in northern China.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">16</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/third-samnite-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/third-samnite-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Third Samnite War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 298–290 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Third Samnite War was fought from 298 to 290 BCE between Rome and the Samnites, who were allied with Etruscans, Umbrians and Gauls.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pyrrhic-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pyrrhic-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pyrrhic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 280–275 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pyrrhic War was fought from 280 to 275 BCE between Rome and Pyrrhus, king of Epirus, who came to Italy to help the Greek city of Tarentum.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/chremonidean-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/chremonidean-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Chremonidean War</span><span class="enc-type">War · c. 267–261 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Chremonidean War (c. 267–261 BCE) was a conflict in which Athens, Sparta and their allies, backed by Ptolemy II of Egypt, tried to end Macedonian domination of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/first-punic-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">First Punic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 264–241 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The First Punic War was fought in 264–241 BCE between Carthage and Rome, mainly over Sicily.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kalinga-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kalinga-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kalinga War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 261 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kalinga War was the Maurya Empire's conquest of Kalinga under Ashoka, dated on the site to 261 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/third-syrian-war"><span class="enc-name">Third Syrian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 246–241 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Third Syrian War (246–241 BCE), also called the Laodicean War, was fought between Ptolemy III of Egypt and the Seleucid king Seleucus II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mercenary-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mercenary-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mercenary War</span><span class="enc-type">War · Revolt · 241–238 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mercenary War was a revolt by Carthage's unpaid mercenary army and its Libyan subjects from 241 to 238 BCE, following the First Punic War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cleomenean-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cleomenean-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cleomenean War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 229–222 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cleomenean War was fought from 229 to 222 BCE between Sparta under King Cleomenes III and the Achaean League.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/social-war-220-217-bce"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/social-war-220-217-bce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Social War (220–217 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">War · 220–217 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Social War of 220–217 BCE was fought between the Hellenic League led by Philip V of Macedon and the Aetolian League, joined by Sparta and Elis.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/fourth-syrian-war"><span class="enc-name">Fourth Syrian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 219–217 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Fourth Syrian War (219–217 BCE) was fought between the Seleucid king Antiochus III and Ptolemy IV of Egypt for control of Coele-Syria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hannibals-crossing-of-the-alps"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hannibals-crossing-of-the-alps.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hannibal's crossing of the Alps</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 218 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">Hannibal's crossing of the Alps was the march of a Carthaginian army, including war elephants, from Iberia over the Alps into Italy in 218 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/second-punic-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Second Punic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 218–201 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Second Punic War was fought from 218 to 201 BCE between Carthage and Rome.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-macedonian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/first-macedonian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">First Macedonian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 214–205 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The First Macedonian War was fought between Rome and Philip V of Macedon, who had allied with Hannibal during the Second Punic War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/anabasis-of-antiochus-iii"><span class="enc-name">Anabasis of Antiochus III</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 212–205 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Anabasis of Antiochus III was the great eastern campaign of the Seleucid king Antiochus III from 212 to 205 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/fifth-syrian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fifth-syrian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Fifth Syrian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 202–198 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Fifth Syrian War, fought in 202–198 BCE, was a conflict between the Seleucid Empire under Antiochus III and the Ptolemaic kingdom.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-macedonian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/second-macedonian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Second Macedonian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 200–197 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Second Macedonian War was fought between Rome and Philip V of Macedon from 200 to 197 BCE.</span></a></li></ul></section>
